Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 16:53:51 2026 -0400

    skill: #11144 Iter 32 — G5 close: Step 1c/1d become sub-skill references in place
    
    Operator: "This is a step in the cycle right? So it make sense to
    create these as Subskill, but remain in place."
    
    The Step 1c (Resume From Working State) and Step 1d (Interval Sync)
    H3s in dm/verifier L2 instructions.md were inlined directly, creating
    the orphan-feel in composed CLAUDE.md (mid-cycle H3s in a Step Nx form
    when everything else around them uses the canonical step:cycle/<id>
    form). The richer sub-skill bodies already existed at
    references/sub-skills/common/{resume-working-state,interval-sync}.md
    but weren't being referenced from L2.
    
    Replaced both inlined H3-blocks with `→ run sub-skill:` markers at the
    same call-site location (operator: "remain in place"). The sub-skill
    bodies are now the single source of truth; agent Reads them at runtime
    per the canonical lazy-load pattern.
    
    Net delta:
    - references/roles/dm/instructions.md: −12 lines
    - references/roles/verifier/instructions.md: −12 lines
    - DM composed CLAUDE.md: 734 → 724 (−10)
    - Verifier composed CLAUDE.md: 726 → 716 (−10)
    - PM + skill composed: unchanged
    
    Behavior preserved: the sub-skill bodies have richer content than the
    L2 inlining did (more detail, generic `[ROLE]` placeholder instead of
    role-specific aliases that substituted to the same value). The two
    existing call-sites for resume-working-state in DM (L1 step:cycle/resume
    at session boot + L2 cycle-runner at per-cycle) remain intentionally
    separate — same sub-skill invoked at two cycle moments.
    
    Closes: G5 (Step 1c/1d orphan numbering)

